Hi BioGeoBEARS users and developer! :)

I am experiencing a puzzeling issue when trying to fit different DIVALIKE and BAYAREALIKE models including a distance matrix.

I have fit models without the "J" parameter but setting "x" to be free. With those models I get estimated values for "d", "e", and "x". Based on those values I fit +J versions of the models. For that I set the initial values of "d" and "e", I give to "J" an starting value of 0.0001, and I set "x" to be free (currently without setting initial values, although I also tried setting as initial value the estimated value in the model without jump-dispersal). Strangely enough, parameter values appear to be the same after optimization. For instance:

MODEL                           LnL     nparam     d           e              j             x           AICc
DIVALIKE+x                -69.8566       3      0.0035   0.0201   0.0000   -0.7659   146.8041
DIVALIKE+J+x            -98.3446       4      0.0035   0.0201   0.0001    0.0000    206.5940
